---
import {Image} from "astro:assets";
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import HomePageLink from "../../components/HomePageLink.astro";
import ContactSection from "../../components/ContactSection.astro";
import RevealScript from "../../components/RevealScript.astro";
import speakingPhoto from "../../assets/about-speaking.png";
import {site} from "@/lib/site";
---

<Layout title="About — Becca Bailey" description={site.tagline}>
  <div>
    <h1 class="mb-6 md:mb-8">About</h1>

    <section
      class="reveal mb-12 grid gap-8 md:mb-16 md:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_min(380px,38%)] md:items-start md:gap-10 lg:gap-12"
    >
      <div class="max-w-prose editorial-prose space-y-4 text-text-muted">
        <p
          class="font-sans text-lg font-medium leading-relaxed text-text md:text-xl"
        >
          {site.tagline}
        </p>
        <p></p>
        <p>
          I'm sometimes not sure what toput here, because I don't have a linear
          career arc that fits into a short elevator pitch. I majored in Music
          Education, and spent the first few years after college graduation
          teaching music and art to elementary students in Chicago and
          Quetzaltenango, Guatemala. I had always been interested in web
          development, but I decided to turn it into a career in 2015. After a
          tech bootcamp and an apprenticeship, I became a front-end focused
          software engineer.
        </p>
        <p>
          Since then, I have been an Engineering Manager, an open source
          maintainer for Victory, a widely-used React data visualization
          library, a design system engineer, and an accessibility advocate. Most
          recently, I had a short stint as a CTO for a legal tech startup,
          helping a founder turn an idea into a real product. I think people are
          the most important part of any tech product, and helping the people
          around me to understand technology is my passion and guiding
          principle.
        </p>
        <div class="pt-2">
          <HomePageLink href="/resume">My professional background</HomePageLink>
        </div>
      </div>

      <figure
        class="m-0 w-full max-w-[380px] justify-self-center md:justify-self-end"
      >
        <Image
          src={speakingPhoto}
          alt="Becca Bailey speaking into a microphone on stage"
          class="image-rounded aspect-[3/4] w-full rounded-md object-cover shadow-soft"
          width={900}
          height={1200}
          loading="eager"
        />
      </figure>
    </section>

    <div class="max-w-prose">
      <section class="reveal mb-12">
        <h2 class="mb-6">Writing &amp; research</h2>
        <div class="editorial-prose space-y-4 text-text-muted">
          <p>
            When I first became a software engineer, a mentor told me that “all
            technical problems are people problems.” Today, I think I would
            rephrase that: all technical problems are systems problems. As it
            turns out, I'm interested in a lot of non-technical systems, too.
          </p>
          <p>
            I write about the strange systems we build around work, creativity,
            technology, and culture. So often, the things we accept as normal
            are just the result of a system that was built intentionally by lots
            of small choices over time, and I find it really fascinating to
            study those choices. In <a href={site.links.substack}
              >Performance Anxiety</a
            >, I use data, research, and a bit of software engineering to
            understand the systems that shape our work and our lives.
          </p>
          <p>
            Lately I've been researching what
            <a href="/making-things/closing-window">twenty years of Ravelry</a>
            can tell us about the changing economics of independent knitting design,
            and what the language on
            <a href="/making-things/language-of-work"
              >tech company careers pages</a
            >
            reveals about the industry and the people who run it.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-8 flex flex-col items-start gap-4">
          <HomePageLink href="/writing">Read my writing</HomePageLink>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
  <ContactSection class="mt-12 md:mt-16" />
  <RevealScript />
</Layout>
